(1) Forged parts shall be classified into Class 1, Class 2, or Class 3 based on the criticality of the part to engine safety and the complexity of the forging process.

(2) Class 1 parts are those where a failure could result in a catastrophic engine failure or a hazard to the aircraft. These parts typically include:
(a) Turbine disks;
(b) Fan blades;
(c) Compressor blades;
(d) Turbine blades;
(e) Shaft segments;
(f) Gear housings;
(g) Main bearing housings;
(h) Combustor liners;
(i) Fuel nozzles;
(j) Igniter plugs;
(k) Thrust reverser actuator components;
(l) Engine mount fittings;
(m) Accessory drive shafts;
(n) Oil pump housings;
(o) Fuel pump housings;
(p) Hydraulic pump housings;
(q) Starter motor housings;
(r) Generator housings;
(s) Control valve bodies;
(t) Check valve bodies;
(u) Relief valve bodies;
(v) Pressure regulator bodies;
(w) Flow control valve bodies;
(x) Temperature control valve bodies;
